# Nougat extraction stub — Medras-MC (McMahon & Prise 2021)

**NOTE:** This is a stub. The Frontiers in Oncology paper is open-access
HTML; text and figures were read directly from the publisher rather than
via a Nougat PDF pass. This file exists to satisfy the LUCID batch
`extraction/` artifact convention.

## Source paper
McMahon SJ, Prise KM. A Mechanistic DNA Repair and Survival Model
(Medras): Applications to Intrinsic Radiosensitivity, RBE and Dose-Rate.
Front. Oncol. 11:689112 (2021).
DOI: 10.3389/fonc.2021.689112
URL: https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fonc.2021.689112/full

## Extraction status
- Full-text: read from Frontiers HTML.
- Figures: 7 numbered figures inspected (Fig 1: schematic; Fig 2: kinetics;
  Fig 3: dose scaling; Fig 4: MID scatter; Fig 5: RBE-vs-LET; Fig 6:
  dose-rate sparing; Fig 7: dose-rate MID predictions).
- Tables: Table 1 (parameters), Table 2 (rate constants + p_complex).
- Equations: Eq 1–12 (mechanistic damage/repair/misrepair formulation +
  linear-quadratic mapping + dose-rate extension).

## Key mechanistic parameters extracted (fed into replication)
- DSB yield: 35 DSB/Gy per typical human cell (5.738 GBP^-1 Gy^-1).
- Complex-damage fraction: p_complex = 0.43 ± 0.02.
- Fast repair rate: lambda_f ≈ 2.1 h^-1.
- Slow repair rate: lambda_s ≈ 0.26 h^-1.
- Nucleus radius: 4.229 μm.
- Chromosome count: 46.
- Direct-damage fraction: directFrac = 0.4.

## What would a real Nougat pass add?
- Structured equation extraction (currently the equations were re-derived
